This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: Advancing spear skill will let you get multi-shots when throwing;
the same for javelin. Advancing polearms should increase your range.
--TheShrewdDude

[2]: Firing a /oFire (maybe /oLightning too) should reveal some terrain
information around the beam --Botje

[3]: Wishing for an artifact that already exists should teleport it to
you --Elliott

[4]: Hello I think cats should SEE INVISIBLE LOL! --lament

[5]: Fresh corpses (only certain monsters, of course; for a short time
- not necessarily the corpse expiration time, though), unseen fire
traps when they go off and lava, wands of fire, and Firebrand, (and
maybe some other things too) should be visible with infravision. I
suppose limiting the range of infravision would be necessary to
compensate. --BenUrban

[6]: if the 'travel' feature is on, you have telecontrol and
teleportitis kicks in while travelling, jump to the destination.
--Botje

[7]: #conduct- Carnivore: The opposite of vegetarian, the carnivore
eats only meat and animal-derived items. --JoshJ

[8]: When sitting on an egg laid by you, you should get the message,
"You sit on the egg. It feels rather comfortable...". --TheShrewdDude

[9]: Buzzards: they're a new type of monster that inhabits the 'B'
group. They'll feed on carrion the same way xorns feed on metal.
They'll spawn randomly in flocks of 2-6, but they'll also come in
greater numbers if there are a lot of corpses on the level. Otherwise,
they're just buffed-up ravens. --TheShrewdDude

[10]: Make the buzzards only show up when multiple (5 or so) corpses of
dead enemies exist on the level, and they leave spontaneously a random
number of turns later (50-200 or so) after eating them all. While
hallucinating, they appear as giant flying vacuum cleaners for the
dungeon. --JoshJ

[11]: Ring of strangulation. After 10 turns of wearing it, you get
gangrene (You feel deathly sick!). Typically generated cursed, of
course. --JoshJ

[12]: Supply and demand: The more available an item has been throughout
the game (or at least in a particular shop), the cheaper it will be
when sold, and vice-versa. This should take into account whether the
items are just lying about, in the possession of a monster, in a
container, or belonging to you. --TheShrewdDude

[13]: Burying your pet (or a dead human) should give you a substantial
bonus to alignment and luck. Priests and other friendly humans should
bury your corpse if you die (so that it's not just sitting under the
ghost). If a priest does this, your ghost does not spawn; rather, the
priest guards the bonespile. --TheShrewdDude

[14]: When you die, the force of you collapsing to the ground should
smash fragile items. This should also happen in circumstances like
passing out, falling down the stairs, and sinking to the ground.
--TheShrewdDude

[15]: Padded sack: It has properties akin to an oilskin sack, but will
not smash fragile items inside when thrown or otherwise abused. Yet
another bag to distinguish from, and also a good alternative to the
regular means of storing your glass cancellation wands! --TheShrewdDude

[16]: Cloaks, towels, and similar large fabric items should be able to
be makeshift sacks. This would be done via the #tie command, which
could also have some functionality with regards to rope. --JoshJ

[17]: Greasing Fire Brand will not work; a charge of the can is used up
and you get the message: "The grease catches on fire as you put it on
the flaming sword!" --TheShrewdDude

[18]: Dragons should mate together to form combinations. D - a dragon
(baby purple dragon) --TheShrewdDude

[19]: The same with other coloured/elemental creatures, such as winter
wolves and hell hounds. I won't go into specifics. --TheShrewdDude

[20]: Specifics, such as a winter wolf cub mating with an adult gold
dragon, are best left up to the reader. --JoshJ

[21]: For example, the above mating combination might produce a dog
egg. --TheShrewdDude

[22]: Zapping undead turning spells at Death should damage him
--Rapidfire

[23]: For more political correctness, change female watchmen to
watchwomen. --TheShrewdDude


